Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:02:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Only suggest public sets from the brief's own universe

The setup AI now names the brief's universe (setUniverse, one of the
platform universe labels: contemporary, historical, fantasy,
science-fiction, supernatural), and each public set line shows its own
universe. The server keeps only suggested sets in that universe and logs
any it drops, so a modern police stop can no longer get a fantasy desert
path. Public sets with no universe label are not offered (logged), since
they cannot be checked. setUniverse is not sent on to the Studio.

Real AI check (5 calls, 10 Nov): police stop -> 3 modern park paths,
car mechanic -> none (no garage set exists), hotel -> 3 hotel lobby views,
dwarf blacksmith -> 3 Dwarven Depths sets, 1940s radio operator -> 3
1940s sets. No set needed dropping.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
